{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns","id":1559632,"title":"Thinking about Patterns...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-26T04:02:55-07:00","id":1559632,"title":"Thinking about Patterns...","content":"Tass, mana, resonance, and magic.<br /> <br /> And patterns.<br /> <br /> I think there is some confusion about what Tass is, and I wonder if a theory of mana can expand into a theory of magic...<br /> <br /> But first, I am curious what people think about patterns. In 1e core there is a spell which allows you to tear apart a material pattern and get mana. I think a Matter spell, which suggests that basic material objects contain mana, or at least are held together by mana. Such that the act of tearing them apart releases the mana. This was not republished in the 2e core, either because the metaphysics has changed, or because game balance suggests that limiting access to mana is a good thing. But you can use Death to do something similar to a living pattern (a la Devouring the Slain). That along with blood sacrifices - killing a creature is described <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's death releases mana from its pattern. </div> </div> </div>Then you have Tass seemingly forming in material patterns based around the matter near a Hallow, and (alongside resonance, the general vibe of the area). <br /> <br /> Platonic Form describing &quot;mana behaving as it does within Tass&quot;<br /> <br /> And Eidolon forming mana into the complex &quot;Prime patterns within living beings and environments&quot;.<br /> <br /> So do think there is a Create Tass spell, possibly as a Compelling spell (at a Hallow where there is untapped mana) or a weaving(?) version with mana from another source... Maybe as a reach effect of Channel mana? Lasting by default (like Destroy Tass).<br /> <br /> But is there also space for a Weaving/Patterning effect Transform Tass? Changing either the resonance or physical nature of some Tass, possibly making it into food, or something safe (if it came from a tainted Hallow). <br /> <br /> On the other side, Spells as mana, not solidified as Tass but dynamic expressions of pure mana, like a plasma to Tass's crystalization. Prime already has effects it can do to spells... Supernal Dispellation, but what about the patterns of non-supernal magic, can mana be transformed into the pattern of Cruac? Or the Alchemy of a Promethean? Would it require other arcana aswell? (Since you clearly wouldn't allow a Prime spell to create a Time effect just because magic is in the purview).<br /> <br /> Magic as mana suggests the ability to drain a magical effect of its power by sucking the mana out, or otherwise disrupting it. Would Prime be able to disrupt Alchemy? Would Vitae be a solid type of Tass whose pattern can be destoryed (perhaps with Death+Life) to release mana? What other possibilities does looking at things in terms of pure patterns evoke?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T05:28:12-07:00","id":1559634,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't personally go with the idea of a spell being &quot;made&quot; of mana just from a general preference for spells to not have some kind of materialist intermediary component that creates their effect. The spell doesn't exist in the Phenomenal; it is an act of arrangement in the Supernal that locally changes the default state of what the Phenomenal is. You don't make a thing hotter by taking hold of its atoms and shaking them up, you alter the platonic basis of how hot it is.<br /> <br /> Because mana is described as the palpable bleed of the Supernal into the Fallen World, that <i>might</i> have instances where a bit of mana is evident in a subject with an active spell upon it (although I would argue insufficient to constitute a point of mana to be transferred into a mage's pattern), but the mana is not the substance of the spell. It's more like waste heat from a machine in operation.<br /> <br /> (Also not a case where the mana is a thing that gives the spell away under most circumstances, because Sight can just skip straight to seeing the Supernal process that is the spell. At best, there might be cases where a spell that has been veiled happens to leave waste mana that can still be picked up, and otherwise it's an observation made by mages obsessed with the mystery of how mana even exists in the Fallen World.)<br /> <br /> Sacrifice and scouring are described as drawing mana from a pattern, and I'm inclined to reconcile this in terms of &quot;something about the nature of life as a phenomenon inherently makes it a subject of Supernal bleed&quot; and &quot;something about the nature of deliberately destroying life makes <i>that</i> a subject of Supernal bleed&quot;.<br /> <br /> With mana understood as a phenomenon of the Supernal expressing itself in the Fallen, and spells considered in terms other than being matrices of mana inducing physical results, you wouldn't be able to emulate effects of other non-Supernal sorceries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T05:51:14-07:00","id":1559635,"title":"","content":"I should say, I am taking Tass as *not* being a natural object infused with mana - which i can see a reading implied in the core book section on Hallows, but rather that is is mana mininicing the patterns (and resonance) in the vicinity of a Hallow.<br /> <br /> And the Platonic Form doesn't create Tass (because a Tass object is pretty solid and re-usable) but it is close enough to be useful, just dissolves after it runs out of mana...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T08:10:10-07:00","id":1559637,"title":"","content":"Some general notes:<br /> <br /> 1. Siphon Integrity, the core 1e spell for getting Mana from things that don't have discrete points of Mana invested in them from spells or other processes, only allowed a mage to use it to take Mana directly into their own Pattern once a day, only gleaned one point of Mana per three full points of Structure damage inflicted, and was a Prime 4 spell that always rolled for Paradox. Given that Devouring the Slain still exists and engages with the limits on Scouring, I think it's less likely that it wasn't ported for game balance reasons and more likely that it either got cut for wordcount in an early draft, wasn't considered a priority for the writer in charge of Prime spells for the corebook, or was considered to need conjunctional Arcana in an edition where the corebook's focus was on spells that only needed one Arcanum to cast.<br /> <br /> 2. Patterns are described in 1e as the mystical &quot;body&quot; of a phenomenon describing the Arcana of which it is composed and in 2e as the aggregate Supernal symbols corresponding to a phenomenon (that aggregate itself made up of individual Forms). Tome of the Pentacle introduces the concept of lacunae, which (under normal circumstances) prevents temporal sympathy from being used to look further back in a subject's past due to that subject not existing in its current form even in a vastly different state \u2014 the straightforward example provided is that you can't simply take a rubber object and use Postcognition to look at the tree it was cast from, so in a practical sense destroying anything necessarily destroys its Pattern.<br /> <br /> 3. The Mage/Mummy crossover material in the Dark Eras Companion's <i>Princes of the Conquered Land</i> describes Mana as shaping the world (in comparison to Pillars <i>being</i> the world). Scrutiny in Focused Mage Sight allows a mage to enhance their ability to understand a Mystery by spending Mana and observing &quot;the shapes it makes as it sublimates into Fallen reality.&quot; As a phenomenon, Mana falls under the purview of Prime, and Prime is paired with Forces as an Arcanum because both are manifestations of power in the same sense of acting as positive presences in reality \u2014 connecting back to the Pillars and the first point above, they're related to the Ka, the vital force that determines if something is alive. Mana bleeds into the Phenomenal World from Hallows until they scab over from hitting their tass capacity, and Supernal beings in the Supernal World regain Mana daily simply from &quot;being&quot; there (as opposed to being summoned into reality).<br /> <br /> 4. Tass is Mana that fills material forms, which is why Platonic Form describes its effects the way it does; given the third point above, there is no real contradiction in the lateral/more refined conceptual move described in Eidolon, and given the first point above, we may reasonably describe the overall situation as &quot;amounts of Mana too small to typically count as full points flow through the Patterns that describe a given phenomenon.&quot; Signs of Sorcery implies in its section on Mana Batteries that mages can create tass by simply channeling Mana into an object, which causes it to crumble away once its reserves are fulling withdrawn (when using tass normally involves consuming it anyway), so changing the physical form of tass could be managed either by moving the Mana into a new object or using Matter to change its shape and other qualities. Changing the Resonance of a given amount of tass is likely as straightforward as using Prime Weaving a la Geomancy, albeit it's probably less efficient to do so instead of changing the keywords at the source.<br /> <br /> 5. Spells come forth from the Supernal, such that any form of Active Mage Sight can see a spell as it is being cast, though after that point the appropriate Arcana are needed to detect and scrutinize them. Spells that are cast without the benefits of Praxes, Rotes, or Ruling Arcana require Mana regardless of their effects, but within those umbrellas Mana is only needed for particular spells with extreme effects like indefinite duration, healing or dealing aggravated damage, rote quality or automatic dice results, or breaking the natural limits of Traits. Given the fourth point above and the connection of Prime with the Ka, coupled with the limits of magic with regard to souls and the Abyss, disrupting spells is typically limited to turning them off or temporarily blotting them out \u2014 the closest exception that would allow you to meddle in greater detail is Primal Transfer, which only swaps the control of a spell and which does not allow sweeping changes to what the spell does because of how spell control works more generally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T09:31:28-07:00","id":1559638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559637#post1559637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some general notes:<br /> <br /> 1. Siphon Integrity, the core 1e spell for getting Mana from things that don't have discrete points of Mana invested in them from spells or other processes, only allowed a mage to use it to take Mana directly into their own Pattern once a day, only gleaned one point of Mana per three full points of Structure damage inflicted, and was a Prime 4 spell that always rolled for Paradox. Given that Devouring the Slain still exists and engages with the limits on Scouring, I think it's less likely that it wasn't ported for game balance reasons and more likely that it either got cut for wordcount in an early draft, wasn't considered a priority for the writer in charge of Prime spells for the corebook, or was considered to need conjunctional Arcana in an edition where the corebook's focus was on spells that only needed one Arcanum to cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I was misremembering that. Definitely thought it was a Matter spell, but it was nearly 20 years ago and a player of mine was taking out the recycling and Siphoning the integrity to avoid having to use any bun service (also, I couldn't find the PDF on my phone last night, but have the book in front of me now). You're right, it is 1 success per point of mana and 1 damage, ignoring durability. With a cap of 1 mana for each 3 sizes an object has (rounding down), so a size 1 or 2 object doesn't have enough structure to get any mana. And a second use you can channel the mana into someone (or something) else.<br /> <br /> Making it Prime+Matter as a spell might be good (it feels like a Matter spell to me), and counting towards the scouring limit would work. I'm not sure you should always need Prime go get mana (like Blood Sacrifice seems like it is more Life adjacent that Prime... And Spirit/Mind/Death can make a familiar bond, which then let's you convert essence to mana freely without Prime bring involved...) <br /> <br /> So you're probably right about it bring cut for word count. Thank you.<br /> <br /> Also, I notice the spell Create Tass is in the 1e core. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Patterns are described in 1e as the mystical &quot;body&quot; of a phenomenon describing the Arcana of which it is composed and in 2e as the aggregate Supernal symbols corresponding to a phenomenon (that aggregate itself made up of individual Forms). Tome of the Pentacle introduces the concept of lacunae, which (under normal circumstances) prevents temporal sympathy from being used to look further back in a subject's past due to that subject not existing in its current form even in a vastly different state \u2014 the straightforward example provided is that you can't simply take a rubber object and use Postcognition to look at the tree it was cast from, so in a practical sense destroying anything necessarily destroys its Pattern.<br /> <br /> 3. The Mage/Mummy crossover material in the Dark Eras Companion's <i>Princes of the Conquered Land</i> describes Mana as shaping the world (in comparison to Pillars <i>being</i> the world). Scrutiny in Focused Mage Sight allows a mage to enhance their ability to understand a Mystery by spending Mana and observing &quot;the shapes it makes as it sublimates into Fallen reality.&quot; As a phenomenon, Mana falls under the purview of Prime, and Prime is paired with Forces as an Arcanum because both are manifestations of power in the same sense of acting as positive presences in reality \u2014 connecting back to the Pillars and the first point above, they're related to the Ka, the vital force that determines if something is alive. Mana bleeds into the Phenomenal World from Hallows until they scab over from hitting their tass capacity, and Supernal beings in the Supernal World regain Mana daily simply from &quot;being&quot; there (as opposed to being summoned into reality). </div> </div> </div>I kinda like the attempt to address the metaphysics of mana vs pillars. And patterns changing with time to be different symbols, like a cow's skin, to leather (a worked material) presumably going through a change seems valid for why the arcana which can affect it also change over time.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Tass is Mana that fills material forms, which is why Platonic Form describes its effects the way it does; given the third point above, there is no real contradiction in the lateral/more refined conceptual move described in Eidolon, and given the first point above, we may reasonably describe the overall situation as &quot;amounts of Mana too small to typically count as full points flow through the Patterns that describe a given phenomenon.&quot; Signs of Sorcery implies in its section on Mana Batteries that mages can create tass by simply channeling Mana into an object, which causes it to crumble away once its reserves are fulling withdrawn (when using tass normally involves consuming it anyway), so changing the physical form of tass could be managed either by moving the Mana into a new object or using Matter to change its shape and other qualities. Changing the Resonance of a given amount of tass is likely as straightforward as using Prime Weaving a la Geomancy, albeit it's probably less efficient to do so instead of changing the keywords at the source. </div> </div> </div>Mana that fills materials forms sounds like a mana battery, which is distinctly not the same thing as Tass.<br /> <br /> Tass is described as solid mana, much the same as mana is described as liquid tass. <br /> <br /> And the section on mana batteries, thank you for bringing my attention to it. Specifically states &quot;channel mana into a physical form&quot; which is open to interpretation. It seems more like it is describing the Create Tass spell from 1e which creates a new physical form out of the mana, and that physical form dissipates once all the mana is gone (the same as with a Platonic Form, and distinct from Siphon Integrity and Mana Battery, where the objects survive - even if damaged in the case of Siphon Integrity).<br /> <br /> So I think there is an entirely consistent reading (especially given the Create Tass spell in 1e which is as weaker version of Platonic Form, or Platonic Form is Create Tass and Phantasm merged into one spell - which is good because Phantasms as illusions feel off for the Arcanum with Truth in its purview... But I digress) for Tass to be mana as an object, rather than mana in an object. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Spells come forth from the Supernal, such that any form of Active Mage Sight can see a spell as it is being cast, though after that point the appropriate Arcana are needed to detect and scrutinize them. Spells that are cast without the benefits of Praxes, Rotes, or Ruling Arcana require Mana regardless of their effects, but within those umbrellas Mana is only needed for particular spells with extreme effects like indefinite duration, healing or dealing aggravated damage, rote quality or automatic dice results, or breaking the natural limits of Traits. Given the fourth point above and the connection of Prime with the Ka, coupled with the limits of magic with regard to souls and the Abyss, disrupting spells is typically limited to turning them off or temporarily blotting them out \u2014 the closest exception that would allow you to meddle in greater detail is Primal Transfer, which only swaps the control of a spell and which does not allow sweeping changes to what the spell does because of how spell control works more generally. </div> </div> </div>Mana naturally flowing into your spells (except when improvising with common/inferior arcana) via your soul seems fine. Your soul can be attuned to generate pure mana through legacy attainments, so having it allow mana become spell-like (dynamic) patterns seems fine, and having extra mana requirements for spells where extra damage of indefinite duration are required would make perfect sense.<br /> <br /> The only thing I can think of that doesn't make sense is how Sophis work to reclaim spend mana as it is dissiapting into the background... <br /> <br /> Even with that, allowing a Supernal Dispellation which creates mana by ripping apart a spell would be the natural outcome... Or describing Celestial Fire's ability to destroy/dissipate mana, identical to Destroy Tass as being able to erode a spell... The fact that there is no rule allowing you to partially erode a spell, reducing it's spell factors one a one for one basis, is one limitation of Prime I'm not sure I like... <br /> <br /> Dissonance can do it, so I don't see the issue with Prime 4 Unravelling being able to do it aswell... Maybe 1 mana +1 reach go undo a reach? Given how Prime 4 mages already have access to Supernal Dispellation, it don't think it would be the worst. Primal Transfer let's the caster transfer spell control to another mage - who can then reduce the spell factors... So I think doing the same by force would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T10:40:17-07:00","id":1559640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559638#post1559638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana that fills materials forms sounds like a mana battery, which is distinctly not the same thing as Tass.</div> </div> </div> </div>That phrasing is directly from the corebook's section on Hallows, describing the means of harvesting Mana from them that is not performing oblations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tass is described as solid mana, much the same as mana is described as liquid tass. </div> </div> </div>Those descriptions are in quotations to represent the fact that tass is discrete substantial objects, much like how &quot;liquidity&quot; is the term used in economics for the convertibility of assets \u2014 you generally can't buy a hamburger with a painting, but you can spend its value in cash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the section on mana batteries, thank you for bringing my attention to it. Specifically states &quot;channel mana into a physical form&quot; which is open to interpretation. It seems more like it is describing the Create Tass spell from 1e which creates a new physical form out of the mana, and that physical form dissipates once all the mana is gone (the same as with a Platonic Form, and distinct from Siphon Integrity and Mana Battery, where the objects survive - even if damaged in the case of Siphon Integrity). </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is that &quot;channel Mana into a physical form to create tass&quot; is using Channel Mana on something that doesn't have a Mana pool of its own; the description of the effects of using it up are consistent with 1e's description of using Channel Mana to remove Mana from tass. 1e had more detailed mechanics for tass, including how long tass in the form of perishable consumable objects would keep, so evidently tass being &quot;solid&quot; Mana does not exempt it from behaving like ordinary material outside the context of constructs like Platonic Forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing I can think of that doesn't make sense is how Sophis work to reclaim spend mana as it is dissiapting into the background... </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're referring to here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even with that, allowing a Supernal Dispellation which creates mana by ripping apart a spell would be the natural outcome... </div> </div> </div>Any given spell may &quot;generate&quot; Mana with exceptional success, which we may attribute to the &quot;coming forth&quot; of the spell from its Imago formation as visible via Display of Power or in the moment of casting from Active Mage Sight \u2014 the net +1 Mana on top of any spent on the spell proper effectively being &quot;leakage&quot; from its transition from abstract to concrete phenomenon, with the expenditures being necessary to push more &quot;out&quot; from the Supernal World as adjusted by your Path, Legacy, training, practice, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or describing Celestial Fire's ability to destroy/dissipate mana, identical to Destroy Tass as being able to erode a spell... </div> </div> </div>It has that ability for the same reason it has the ability to strike foes in Twilight or burn flammable objects \u2014 it's attacking at the metaphysical core of the phenomenon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that there is no rule allowing you to partially erode a spell, reducing it's spell factors one a one for one basis, is one limitation of Prime I'm not sure I like...<br /> <br /> Dissonance can do it, so I don't see the issue with Prime 4 Unravelling being able to do it aswell... Maybe 1 mana +1 reach go undo a reach? Given how Prime 4 mages already have access to Supernal Dispellation, it don't think it would be the worst. Primal Transfer let's the caster transfer spell control to another mage - who can then reduce the spell factors... So I think doing the same by force would be nice. </div> </div> </div>Mages already have a harder time dynamically reducing their own spell factors than simply ending them \u2014 an instant action versus a reflexive one \u2014 so between that, the connection of spellcasting with an exercise of Will, and Imperial Mysteries making &quot;Alter the spell factors, target, and other details of a spell of the Arcanum&quot; a generic example of an Entities spell, I don't think it much benefits the game to allow Prime to meddle at a more detailed level than &quot;the spell works&quot; and &quot;the spell is being lent to someone else&quot; without archmastery or Abyssal meddling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-26T12:09:53-07:00","id":1559641,"title":"","content":"The simplest way I would describe the Platonic Form spell is that the nature of mana as a Supernal energy and the Prime Arcanum as covering the purview of Truth is that it's possible to mould mana into a framework of the essential Form of a thing in a way that, by virtue of existing in the Phenomenal World, can be used to accomplish the functions of that thing. I view the fact that points of mana need to be spent for those otherwise mundane actions in terms of action itself being a transitional thing that sets mana in motion, or perhaps by a property of a thing that the framework can only effectively emulate with mana flowing through it.<br /> <br /> (I tend to view that &quot;mana as framework&quot; thing actually kind of literally, as basically &quot;Platonic Form makes things that look like Dr Strange magic from the MCU&quot;, as the way to realise the point that the subjects are obviously magical unless masked with holograms. Even with regards to the idea that the semiotics might differ between mages, it still comes back to a point that it's not so much being able to say something about how mana relates to objects as it is how mana can be shaped around the idea of objects, will still being pretty obviously a handful of manifested mana.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T00:30:55-07:00","id":1559642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559640#post1559640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My interpretation is that &quot;channel Mana into a physical form to create tass&quot; is using Channel Mana on something that doesn't have a Mana pool of its own; the description of the effects of using it up are consistent with 1e's description of using Channel Mana to remove Mana from tass.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this have the side effect that you can channel 1 mana into an object (size 20? There doesn't seem to be a limit).<br /> <br /> And then upon channeling the mana back out the object disintegrates like it has been Unmade (or per the rules described in 1e core, 1 mana removed reduces the structure by 1, so it slowly disintegrates?)<br /> <br /> While also allowing you to protect against Matter spells such as Annihilate Matter, by making it a magical object which requires an extra reach for a Master of Matter to Unmake?<br /> <br /> Your interpretation is definitely at odds with the 1e description of Create Tass. Which talks about creating a dog shaped piece of Tass as an example and having it curl up beside a fire place... But being inanimate.<br /> <br /> Edit: damn, lost my edit.<br /> <br /> I think the conclusion was, what does Destroy Tass do in your opinion?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559641#post1559641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Platonic Form makes things that look like Dr Strange magic from the MCU&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always thought of Display of Power as making spells look line Dr Strange, while Platonic Form could be more like Green Lantern... But maybe what &quot;obviously magical&quot; looks like could be filtered through the character's Nimbus...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 04-27-2026, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T02:02:17-07:00","id":1559644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559640#post1559640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> Mages already have a harder time dynamically reducing their own spell factors than simply ending them \u2014 an instant action versus a reflexive one \u2014 so between that, the connection of spellcasting with an exercise of Will, and Imperial Mysteries making &quot;Alter the spell factors, target, and other details of a spell of the Arcanum&quot; a generic example of an Entities spell, I don't think it much benefits the game to allow Prime to meddle at a more detailed level than &quot;the spell works&quot; and &quot;the spell is being lent to someone else&quot; without archmastery or Abyssal meddling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a seperate but interesting question.<br /> <br /> Spells can naturally erode of time, so reducing spell factors (for an unsafely relinquished spell) would qualify as a Compelling practice, right?<br /> <br /> I haven't read the Entities practice from IM, but I presume that let's you increase spell factors. <br /> <br /> Dissonance is almost the definition of &quot;not natural&quot; as it envokes the Abyss, but unsafely relinquished spells (while using the paradox rules) is not Abyssal.. but reading those rules, it only allows a change of subject, change in reach effects or imposing a condition (I think we have Word of God that this isn't Abyssal, and just re-used the paradox rules for word count, so I wouldn't be adding Abyssal environmental conditions or summoning Entities from the Abyss). Not changing spell factors... Though the result is similar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-27T12:25:41-07:00","id":1559651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1559632-thinking-about-patterns?p=1559644#post1559644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spells can naturally erode of time, so reducing spell factors (for an unsafely relinquished spell) would qualify as a Compelling practice, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells pick up effective Paradox Reach with time, which can undo Reach effects. Dissonance reduces spell factors directly but is a Withstood roll of Integrity with dice tricks for headcount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read the Entities practice from IM, but I presume that let's you increase spell factors. </div> </div> </div>It's the same Practice that lets you create Demesnes without a soul stone, create new supernatural templates, password-protect a subject's sympathetic ties, create Artifacts, and otherwise mess with the way the Arcana interact with a subject. Dynamics spells, the Practice one dot lower, can be used to create spells that spread like viruses or memes, altering timelines all at once toward a desired outcome, or making substances that have whatever properties they need for their current purpose.<br /> <br /> Cross-splat comparison is tricky at the best of times, but there's a reason other splats also don't get more involved with meddling with the products of their own powers than counteraction, dismissal, or interaction with the end product. Powers to meddle with expressions of another being's Will at the root level are above the pay grade of Travelers' Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}